# 20260827 scaling CC and LL down together at fixed zeta, to reach the defect regime.
#
# xi_N = sqrt(LL/(2*CC)) depends only on the RATIO, so scaling both by 1/a leaves the
# defect core size untouched at 2.0 lattice units while raising the one number that decides
# whether defects exist at all:
#
#     zeta_eff/CC >~ 0.5-1   (local distortion energy ~ zeta reaching the LdG barrier ~ CC/2)
#
# measured anchors: case C at zeta/CC = 1.8 melted 5.4% of the domain; the L=800 design
# point at 0.125 melted nothing. Here zeta_eff/CC = 0.125*a.
#
# This beats simply raising zeta: same effect on zeta/CC, but u ~ 2*sqrt(zeta*LL)/eta FALLS
# with LL instead of rising, so the Mach number improves rather than degrades, and the
# smaller LL is further from the (xi, tau, LL) numerical stability boundary.
#
# a=1 : CC=0.05 LL=0.4 -> zeta_eff/CC = 0.125
model=confluent-wet
nsteps=40000
nstart=0
ninfo=1000
LX=200
LY=200
bc=0
seed=1001
Gamma=0.05
xi=0.4
CC=0.05
LL=0.4
tau=1.0
rho=40
friction=0.0
zeta=0.0125
angle=0
noise=0.05
initial-order=1
director-config=uniform
defect-sep=0
Dbio=0
chi-config=uniform
chi0=0.5
chi-noise=0
chi-length=0
tau-chi=-1
chi-width=0.15
switch-sign=1
mc=0.5
m0=0.5
tau-m=1e12
pmem=0
pmem-width=1e-3
